  "notes": "{純粋|じゅんすい} is a na-adjective with two main uses: physical purity (unmixed, unadulterated) and personal innocence or sincerity.\n\nFORMS:\n- {純粋|じゅんすい}な: pure (attributive)\n- {純粋|じゅんすい}に: purely (adverbial)\n- {純粋|じゅんすい}さ: purity (noun form)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {純粋|じゅんすい}な{気持|きも}ち: pure feelings\n- {純粋|じゅんすい}な{心|こころ}: pure heart\n- {純粋|じゅんすい}{培養|ばいよう}: pure culture (scientific)\n- {純粋|じゅんすい}{数学|すうがく}: pure mathematics\n- {純粋|じゅんすい}に{楽|たの}しむ: enjoy purely, simply enjoy\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {単純|たんじゅん}: simple (shares {純|じゅん} but means uncomplicated, not 'pure')\n- {素朴|そぼく}: simple, naive, unsophisticated\n- {無垢|むく}: pure, innocent (literary/poetic)",
